<Legal title="Terms of service" description="The terms for Recordly accounts, cloud sharing and Cloud subscriptions.">
  <h2>1. Scope and agreement</h2>
  <p>These terms govern the hosted Recordly services provided by Recordly. Read them together with the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/billing">billing and refund policy</a> before using a hosted account or purchasing Cloud. The open-source desktop software remains governed by its applicable software licences; these terms do not remove rights granted by those licences.</p>
  <p>You must have the authority and legal capacity to agree to these terms. If you need a parent’s or guardian’s permission under applicable law, involve them before using a hosted account. A paid subscription must be purchased by someone authorised to enter the payment agreement. If you use Recordly for an organisation, you must be authorised to act for it.</p>
  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <p>Provide accurate account information, protect your sign-in methods and tell us if your account appears compromised. Account features and paid access are linked to your verified Recordly account, not a particular installation or a matching checkout email address. Do not share another person’s credentials, impersonate someone or try to access another account’s private library.</p>
  <h2>3. Your recordings and permissions</h2>
  <p>You retain ownership of the content you create or upload. You give the operator and its service providers the limited permission needed to store, process, display and deliver content through the features you use, including generating thumbnails, serving sharing links and maintaining permitted recovery copies. We do not acquire ownership of your recordings.</p>
  <p>You are responsible for having the rights and permissions required to record screens, people, voices, meetings, copyrighted works and personal or confidential information. Recording consent requirements vary by location. Upload only content you are authorised to share.</p>
  <h2>4. Sharing and local copies</h2>
  <p>Anyone who obtains an unprotected sharing link may be able to watch and redistribute it. Password protection adds an access check but cannot prevent an authorised viewer from copying content. Do not treat a public link as confidential storage. The service hosts published media; it is not a backup service for editable Recordly projects. Keep your own copies of important work.</p>
  <h2>5. Free and Cloud services</h2>
  <p>The desktop recording and editing features remain available under the software’s licence. Optional hosted services have the limits displayed in the app and at checkout. At launch, Free allows five stored cloud recordings of up to 1 GB each, normally expiring after 14 days. Cloud includes unlimited cloud storage and playback bandwidth, with up to 10 GB per recording. Upload rate and abuse protections still apply. GB means one billion bytes. Reserved and incomplete uploads may count toward capacity.</p>
  <p>Cloud recordings granted no-expiry retention keep that retention after cancellation. A verified upgrade also grants that retention to eligible completed recordings still stored at the time of upgrade. This does not recover already expired or deleted files. After paid access ends, new uploads follow the Free limits; retained recordings still count toward stored capacity and applicable recording counts.</p>
  <p>“No expiry” means no scheduled deletion solely because of age or subscription cancellation. It does not prevent deletion you request, lawful removal or removal necessary to address serious abuse. It is not a guarantee of uninterrupted service or a separate disaster-recovery copy.</p>
  <h2>6. Prices, renewals and cancellation</h2>
  <p>Cloud is a recurring subscription. Current pricing and any promotional offers appear in Recordly. Checkout displays the amount, currency, interval and any applicable taxes before you pay. Your payment provider or bank may apply currency-conversion fees.</p>
  <p>Your subscription renews automatically at its stated interval until cancelled. Use <strong>Manage subscription</strong> in Recordly to access Stripe’s billing portal. A normal cancellation stops renewal and keeps paid access until the end of the current paid period. Uninstalling the app, signing out or deleting a recording does not cancel billing. See <a href="/billing">billing and refunds</a> for further details.</p>
  <p>We will give advance notice of a material price or plan change before it applies to a renewal, with the opportunity to cancel. We will not charge a different price for an already-paid period without your agreement or remove retention already granted solely because a plan changes.</p>
  <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not use the service for unlawful content, child sexual abuse material, threats, harassment, infringement, non-consensual intimate material, malware or disclosure of information you are not entitled to publish. Do not evade storage limits or security controls, conduct unauthorised testing, interfere with other users, automate abusive traffic or resell access without permission.</p>
  <p>We may investigate reports and restrict access or remove content where reasonably necessary to meet legal obligations, protect people or prevent serious abuse. Where lawful and practical, we will explain the reason and offer a way to challenge an error. We will not use this power to remove statutory refund rights.</p>
  <h2>8. Payments that fail or are disputed</h2>
  <p>Paid upload privileges depend on a valid, paid subscription. Failed payments, cancellation taking effect, refunds or disputes may suspend those privileges while billing is resolved. A payment-related restriction does not by itself reverse retention already granted to completed recordings. Contact support if the account or billing status is wrong; do not start multiple subscriptions to bypass a restriction.</p>
  <h2>9. Availability, changes and closure</h2>
  <p>We aim to operate the service reliably, but outages, maintenance and service-provider failures can occur. We may make reasonable service changes. If we plan to discontinue hosted storage, we will give reasonable advance notice and an opportunity to export available media where practical, and address prepaid services and refunds in accordance with applicable law.</p>
  <p>Account closure, data deletion and subscription cancellation are different actions. Contact support for help closing an account and removing associated hosted information. We may retain records required by law or necessary to resolve an outstanding matter as explained in the privacy policy.</p>
  <h2>10. Consumer rights and responsibility</h2>
  <p>Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies a guarantee, right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded, including rights under the Australian Consumer Law where it applies. You may be entitled to a repair, replacement, refund, cancellation or compensation when a service fails a statutory guarantee.</p>
  <p>Subject to those rights, we do not promise that the service will be suitable for every purpose or free of interruptions. Each party remains responsible for its conduct as required by applicable law. These terms do not impose an unlimited indemnity on individual users or require you to waive non-excludable rights.</p>
  <h2>11. Concerns and updates</h2>
  <p>Contact us using the details below about billing, a privacy request, an access restriction, illegal content or another dispute. Tell us enough to identify the account or link without sending passwords or full payment details. Applicable law determines any rights to contact a regulator or seek a legal remedy; these terms do not remove them.</p>
  <p>Material changes will be published with an updated effective date and any notice or acceptance required by law. Changes will not retroactively remove an accrued consumer right or the paid retention already granted under these terms.</p>
